      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables\n    face_value = 1000.0\n    current_one_year_rate = 0.08\n    up_rate = 0.10\n    down_rate = 0.06\n    probability_each = 0.50\n    annual_risk_premium = 0.004\n\n    # Discount the expected year-1 bond value using the current rate,\n    # with the duration risk premium added to each year's rate.\n    expected_year1_discount_factor = (\n        probability_each / (1 + up_rate + annual_risk_premium)\n        + probability_each / (1 + down_rate + annual_risk_premium)\n    )\n    bond_value = (\n        face_value\n        * expected_year1_discount_factor\n        / (1 + current_one_year_rate + annual_risk_premium)\n    )\n\n    # Return the valuation rounded to three decimal places\n    return round(bond_value, 3)\n```",
